# Emergency intake — submit-to-escalation sequence + P4 sweep (ADR-040/043)
# careOS — docs/diagrams/emergency-intake-sequence.mmd

sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Anonymous caller
  participant P as PublicEmergencyController
  participant SVC as EmergencyIntakeService
  participant DB as tenant emergency_requests
  participant Q as BullMQ emergency-escalation
  participant W as EmergencyIntakeWorker
  participant RT as Realtime/SSE

  C->>P: POST /public/emergency/requests (slug, callerPhone, description, location)
  P->>SVC: submitPublic()
  SVC->>SVC: callerPhoneIndex = normalize(callerPhone)
  alt phone present and open request inside EMERGENCY_DEDUPE_SECONDS
    SVC-->>C: { request: { id, referenceNumber, duplicate: true } }
  else no recent duplicate
    SVC->>DB: tx: create + RECEIVED event + counter (EMR-…), token hash only
    SVC->>SVC: token returned exactly once
    opt policy.enabled && autoEscalate
      SVC->>Q: add('escalate', {requestId, level:1}, jobId '<id>-1')  delay
    end
    SVC-->>C: { request, trackingToken, contact }
  end

  Note over W,Q: later, each delayed level fires (repeated for levels 2..N)
  Q->>W: escalate job (level k)
  W->>SVC: attemptEscalation(requestId, org, level k)
  SVC->>DB: guarded updateMany (escalationLevel = k-1, status RECEIVED|ESCALATED)
  alt won
    SVC->>SVC: write ESCALATED event + CALL_NOW/await-next-level
    SVC->>Q: add level k+1 job (unless final level)
    SVC->>RT: Emergency.RequestEscalated
  else noop (already acked / a higher level / closed)
  end

  Note over W: repeat maintenance job every EMERGENCY_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS (not in test)
  W->>SVC: reconcileEscalations() — scan open requests + enabled policies
  SVC->>SVC: recompute overdue level (lost-job watchdog) -> attemptEscalation (idempotent)
  W->>SVC: applyRetention() — CLOSED/CANCELLED older than EMERGENCY_RETENTION_DAYS
  SVC->>DB: guarded tx: retainedAt, token='retired:<id>', null caller PII + RETENTION event + audit
  SVC->>RT: Emergency.RequestRetained